These are the files for Life with David, Bare Metal Adventures, Chapter 16, Multi-core, multi-program, multi-memory execution.  
This includes the source, CMakeLists, header, and linker script files for the five demo programs in the chapter, they are:

Demo 1) Transferring execution of core 0 from a C program in FLASH memory to an assembly program in FLASH memory.
Demo 2) Copying an assembly program from FLASH memory to SRAM memory, and then transferring execution of core 0 from a C program in 
        FLASH to the assembly program in SRAM.
Demo 3) Starting Core 1 and transferring into an endless loop inside the C program.  Meanwhile, Core 0 copies the assembly program 
        from FLASH to SRAM, and then transfers execution from the C program in FLASH to the assembly program in SRAM.
Demo 4) Starting Core 1 and transferring into an endless loop inside the C program.  Meanwhile, Core 0 copies the assembly program 
        from FLASH to SRAM, copies a 64 kB dtat file from FLASH to SRAM, and then transfers execution from the C program in FLASH 
        to the assembly program in SRAM.
Demo 5) Putting it all together.  Starting Core 1 and transferring execution into the keyboard display C program in FLASH.  This 
        includes the PIO program and header file needed for the keyboard display.  Meanwhile, Core 0 using the Startup C program, 
        copies the assembly program from FLASH to SRAM, copies a 64 kB data file from FLASH to SRAM, and then transfers execution 
        from the startup C program in FLASH to the assembly program in SRAM.
